dialect protocol
protocol stdio.txt.diff
version 1
schema stdio.txt.diff
start diff

# P2-P3: `protocol::DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff` for `TxtDiff` are derive-generated
# (`#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]`, ../🦀️component.rs) via `🗣️dsl/✨️derive/🦀️component.rs`'s `DslDiff`
# region -- ALREADY real binary before this program touched it, NOT the F6-era
# `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut (confirmed by direct reading: `encode_diff`
# calls `store::pack_rt::encode_document`, never `print_diff`). Unlike the sibling mutations
# facet's `OpBinary` (which forwards to the LIGHT `os_pack::encode_record_body` helper --
# ../../🧬️mutations/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio), `encode_document` wraps the record in
# the FULL `.spk` document container (`🎒️pack/📐️format/🦀️component.rs`, `MAGIC = [0x89,'S','P','K',
# 0x0D,0x0A,0x1A,0x0A]`) -- a real, checksummed, chunk-table-indexed, optionally-deflate-compressed
# random-access file format, not a lightweight per-message frame. Confirmed empirically against a
# real `TxtDiff::encode_diff()` call: `required_flags` bit 0 (`REQUIRED_COMPRESSED`) is genuinely
# set, i.e. deflate compression is genuinely active on real diff payloads, not a theoretical edge
# case.
#
# This file models the one fixed, ALWAYS-present, self-contained structure: the 32-byte
# superblock header (`Header::write_bytes`/`Header::parse`, 🎒️pack/📐️format/🦀️component.rs) --
# magic, format version, feature-flag bitfields, and a self-CRC over the first 20 bytes (the CRC
# value itself is opaque here -- this dialect has no CRC-verification primitive, same
# "structurally irreducible" treatment M2 already gives every other checksum). Every OTHER byte
# of a real `.spk` file (segment table, chunk table, symbol table, the deflate-compressed record
# body itself, and a 84-byte FOOTER magic-scanned backward from EOF, `FOOTER_MAGIC = "SPKFOOT1"`,
# `Footer`/`FOOTER_SIZE`) forms a real random-access, checksum-validated, compressed document
# container -- the SAME category of complexity the user's own decisions and M2's own scope
# (P2-M1/M2 report, "Explicitly excluded from M2") already carve out for DWG's compression
# pipeline and PDF/1.7's full indirect-object graph: an imperative, checksum/compression-driven
# transform, not a declarative fixed layout. `.spk` is furthermore a FRAMEWORK-level container --
# shared verbatim by every `#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]` type in the whole repo, not anything specific
# to `stdio.txt` -- so a full per-segment/footer description belongs at a framework-level
# `pack_format.protocol.semio` file (mirroring M3's own `semio.envelope` precedent), out of this
# per-artifact ticket's ownership boundary (recorded in this report's `mechanism_gaps`). Modeled
# honestly: the 32-byte header IS genuinely, individually byte-walked and validated, field for
# field; everything past it is one opaque tail.
framing magic 0x8953504B0D0A1A0A
header fixed 24
field version_major u16
field version_minor u16
field required_flags u32
field optional_flags u32
field header_crc32 u32
field reserved fixed 8
chain bytes
